We find the discriminant of the quadratic $(x^2 + ax + b + a - 1).$ It is $\left(a^2 - 4(b + a - 1)\right)^2 - 4\left(a^2 - 4(b + a - 1)\right).$ Equating this to zero gives $(a - 2)^2(4b^2 - 4a^2 - 8ab + 8a + 16b - 48) = 0.$ The first factor obviously works, for every $b$ if $a = 2.$ The second factor gives three values of $a.$

These are easy to find; $b = 2,$ numbers between 0 and 1, and $-3/2.$ The sums of $a$ value and $b$ value satisying the polynominal have to be added. We find $2 + 2 + 2 + 1 + 1 - 1 - 3/2 + 0 + 1 - 2  + 1 - 1 + 1/2 + 0 - 0 + 1 = \boxed{4 1/2}.$</ think</ think> <answer>4 1/2</ answer> **Add-on by Ruslan** [asy]
   import graph; size(7.75cm); real lsf=0.5; pen dps=linewidth(0.7)+fontsize(10); defaultpen(dps); pen ds=black; 
draw((0,0)--(-8,10),linewidth(1.2)); draw((-8,10)--(-3,-4),linewidth(1.2)); draw((-3,-4)--(0,0),linewidth(1.2)); draw((0,0)--(-8,10),linewidth(1.2)); 
dot((-8,10),ds); label("$(-8,10)$", (-8.8,10.6),NE*lsf); dot((-3,-4),ds); label("$P_1$",(-3.1,-4.6),NE*lsf); dot((0,0),ds); label("$P_2$", (0,0),NE*lsf); 
clip((xmin,ymin)--(xmin,ymax)--(xmax,ymax)--(xmax,ymin)--cycle);[/asy]
